        "title": "Conformal Mappings and Applications",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Conformal maps are the geometric face of holomorphic functions. They preserve angles and local shape (but not generally area or length). Their power comes from the Riemann Mapping Theorem: any simply connected domain (other than all of ℂ) is conformally equivalent to the unit disk. This means: solving a PDE on a complicated domain reduces to finding the right conformal map, solving on the disk, then transforming back."
    }
